      "writtenOn": "2023-03-02T21:52:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking more along the lines of conditions where we may not even call `charge_manager_refresh` after setting the flag.\n\nIn order to call `charge_manager_refresh` from `charge_manager_set_ceil`, then we\u0027ll need to return true for `is_valid_port` and then also true for `charge_ceil[port][requestor] !\u003d ceil` and `port \u003d\u003d charge_port \u0026\u0026 charge_manager_is_seeded()` \n\nThis functions \"if\" certainly covers `port \u003d\u003d charge_port`.  `is_valid_port` may be implied in a way by the fact that `port \u003d\u003d charge_port`.  I was trying to decide if `left_safe_mode` here implies that `charge_manager_is_seeded` will be true as well.  And then also trying to ensure that `ceil \u003c charge_current` covers the `charge_ceil` check in the other function. \n\nBasically, there are a lot of somewhat similar if\u0027s between these two functions and I want to ensure they approximately match up so the flag set/process/clear is reliable (and ideally readable). \n\nThen I suppose we also could hit an issue of disconnect while the flag is set to true (changing the charge port before the `charge_maanger_refresh` could be called), but that would require a very specifically unfortunate timing window.",
      "parentUuid": "589a482b_a1a216d6",
      "revId": "a1e0797aeeee9230d309db5a830ec579b8fd9ed9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "202fd507_d258adf2",
        "filename": "common/charge_manager.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1306,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-02T23:32:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, charge_manager_force_ceil\u0027s premise as an API is to lower the ceil for the current charge port. It doesn\u0027t need to find a better port, supplier, or PDO. That means most of charge_manager_refresh doesn\u0027t need to be called.\n\nThe only problem I see in not calling charge_manager_refresh is not updating charge_current. I wonder if we should/can update it here. It\u0027s necessarily lower than the current charge_current (because of ceil \u003c charge_current). So, we can simply do\n\n    charge_current \u003d ceil;\n\nWDYT? Actually, if this is accepted, we probably don\u0027t need pd_ceil_enforced[] because the condition at line 882 will be true.",
      "parentUuid": "204f4bcf_da14b06f",
      "revId": "a1e0797aeeee9230d309db5a830ec579b8fd9ed9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
